---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import interview from '../../assets/interview.jpg';
const steps=[['Discovery','Clarify your audience, occasion, purpose, and starting material.'],['Narrative','Find the central idea and the stories that support it.'],['Draft','Develop the structure into a complete spoken message.'],['Revisions','Refine the draft through the feedback process agreed for your project.'],['Optional rehearsal','Discuss support for bringing the written words into the room.']];
---
<Base title="Keynote writing in your voice" description="Develop a keynote with Loren Michaels Harris, from audience discovery and narrative structure to drafting, revisions, and optional rehearsal.">
<section class="wrap service-hero writing-hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">KEYNOTE WRITING WITH LOREN</p><h1>Your ideas.<br/>Your voice.<br/><span class="gold-text">The right words.</span></h1><p>For leaders and speakers preparing an important talk. Bring an idea, a set of notes, or an early draft. Build a keynote your audience can follow and recognize as yours.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=keynote-writing">Discuss your keynote ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="#process">Explore the process ↓</a></div></div><figure class="reveal"><Image src={interview} alt="Loren in an outdoor conversation with a woman beside a film camera" widths={[400,700,1000]} sizes="(max-width:767px) calc(100vw - 40px), 46vw" format="webp" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>A filmed conversation from Loren’s published collection.</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="section light-section"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">GIVE THE MESSAGE A THROUGH-LINE</p><h2>What should they<br/>carry out<br/>of the room?</h2></div><div><p>A strong keynote needs a clear idea, a structure that holds it together, and language that sounds like the person delivering it.</p><p>The writing conversation begins with your audience and occasion. From there, the work moves through narrative structure, a draft, and an agreed revision process.</p><p>Timelines, revision rounds, confidentiality, and ownership terms are confirmed before work begins. Rehearsal support can be discussed separately.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap" id="process"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">FROM DISCOVERY TO DELIVERY</p><h2>Build the talk.<br/>One clear step at a time.</h2></div></div><div class="writing-process">{steps.map(([title,body],i)=><article><span class="number">0{i+1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{body}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="section light-section"><div class="wrap split"><div><p class="eyebrow">LET’S GET SPECIFIC</p><h2>Tell us about<br/>the occasion.</h2></div><div><p>Include the audience, talk length, deadline, and any notes or draft you already have. That context helps define the work and the next conversation.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/?service=keynote-writing">Discuss your keynote ↗</a></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap booking-alternative"><p>Prefer to talk through your ideas? <a href="https://calendly.com/lorenmichaelsharris">Schedule a call with Loren ↗</a></p></section>
</Base>
<style>
.writing-hero figure img{height:auto;max-height:none}.writing-hero h1{font-size:clamp(56px,6vw,88px)}.writing-process article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:48px minmax(0,.8fr) minmax(0,1.2fr);gap:32px;align-items:start;padding-block:30px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.writing-process article:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.writing-process h3,.writing-process p{margin:0}.writing-process p{color:var(--muted)}.writing-process .number{padding-top:9px}@media(max-width:767px){.writing-hero h1{font-size:clamp(52px,12.5vw,78px)}.writing-process article{grid-template-columns:32px minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px 20px}.writing-process p{grid-column:2}}
</style>
